From 8a4e36154be77c11ab2f4d387ffcff7b4854d084 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hou Qi <qi.hou@nxp.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Oct 2025 16:46:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] V4L2VideoDecoder: Disable decoder prioritization
 according to resolutions

Below commit enabled decoder prioritization according to different
resolutions, it causes clips that height is lower than 360 to select
software decoder first. So disable this feature.

commit fda2916b9565074bd8f3133ae6d01eb1ca19700a
Author: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Date:   Mon Mar 31 14:23:05 2025 -0700

    Reland "Enable resolution based priority for src= playbacks."

    This is a reland of commit a808cad79e6993eb45ba6985d40f44366fc3d5f8

    Crash fixed in https://crbug.com/407493654

    Original change's description:
    > Enable resolution based priority for src= playbacks.
    >
    > Data shows this significantly improves rebuffering events and time
    > to first frame for src= playbacks, but is neutral to negative for
    > MSE based playbacks.
    >
    > As a side effect of this change Android will return to allowing
    > platform decoders for low resolution MSE playbacks. I'll monitor
    > gpu crash rates to see if this regresses the improvements gained
    > when we launched the software decoder there.
    >
